Find the smallest positive integer \( x \) that satisfies the system of congruences:
\[
\begin{cases}
x \equiv 2 \pmod{5} \\
x \equiv 3 \pmod{7} \\
x \equiv 4 \pmod{9}
\end{cases}
\]

A fair 12-sided die is rolled repeatedly until the first occurrence of a 7 or 8
is achieved. What is the expected number of rolls required to achieve this in
terms of the probability p of rolling a 7 or 8? \boxed{\frac{12p + 1}{p}}

