Let \(a\), \(b\), and \(c\) be distinct positive integers such that the existence of a solution to the system 
  \begin{align*}
    a + b + c &= n,\\
    ab + bc + ca &= m
  \end{align*}
  implies that \(m \leq 72\). Find the smallest possible value of \(n + m\).
